    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d821">

                <pb facs="1118" n="998" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg998"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">818.6363/112: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Costa Rica</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Davis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San José</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-04-29T11:00:00-06:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 29,
                                1922—11 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 11:20
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>15. My telegram number 10, April 15, 2 p.m.<anchor n="19" xml:id="d821-f1"/>
                    Minister of Foreign Affairs … informed me Special Investigator Esquivel has
                    reported relative to contract of Costa Rica Oil Corporation and according to
                    present plans the President will cancel contract by Executive decree at an early
                    date. Cancellation based on charges one and two reported on page 3 despatch
                    number 274, January 4, 1922.<anchor n="20" xml:id="d821-f2"/> Corporation
                    maintains forfeiture can be declared only after contractor is heard in his
                    defense.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Davis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
